+# Proposals awaiting Justin, from the entropy assessment of ORC and the lab, 7 October 2026
+
+**Status: awaiting Justin. None of these is decided.** Each names what it asks, why the evidence in the two
+repositories cannot settle it, and the recommendation. Work that depends on an answer is drafted as a provisional
+patch and is not applied until he answers. When he does, record the answer below its proposal, dated, and apply or
+drop the patch.
+
+## P1. Is the restart card's reach authorised?
+
+ORC's `AGENTS.md` lists where subprocess access exists and says any new authority needs an explicit human choice.
+`src/adapters/orc-service.ts` also runs git's read commands, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (which downloads packages
+when a release adds them), `node scripts/build.mjs` and `systemctl --user restart orc.service`, for the "Restart ORC
+onto <commit>" card (orchestrator#101). The architecture test approves it; no recorded decision does.
+**Recommended:** authorise exactly those four commands, because Justin approves each restart card and the card exists
+to end restarts only he could do by hand. Then ORC's `AGENTS.md` lists the module.
+
+## P2. May Scope packages reach ntfy through the phone connector?
+
+ORC's `AGENTS.md` says no model or agent reaches the ntfy transport, and that it sends only a title, a summary and the
+one configured tap address. `src/adapters/phone/index.ts` lets an approved package send a title, text, up to five tags
+and any http or https tap address to the installation's topic (orchestrator#184, first used 2 Oct). A link a model
+chooses is an outbound channel (`AGENTS.md`, the lethal trifecta).
+**Recommended:** authorise the connector as built, and say whether its tap address may be any address or only ORC's
+own. It replaced a package's own ntfy client, so it narrowed what came before.
+
+## P3. Which file owns the cap on `STATE.md`, and what is it?
+
+`AGENTS.md` here says about forty content lines; `STATE.md`'s own header says sixty. It was 99 lines on 4 Oct and 405
+on 23 Sep (`FRICTION.md`).
+**Recommended:** forty, owned by `AGENTS.md`, with `STATE.md`'s header pointing there. Nothing records a move to sixty.
+
+## P4. Where does the session-end entropy guard live?
+
+The 4 Oct decision keeps "entropy guard at session end" but does not place it.
+**Recommended:** one guard for both repositories at `skills/session-coherence-guard/SKILL.md` here, pointed at from
+both `AGENTS.md` files, because sessions span both and record state only in this Scope's `STATE.md`, and this is the
+central Scope for code quality (4 Oct). ORC loads a Scope's skills only by installation approval, so ORC's agents do
+not receive it.
+
+## P5. Where are Justin's decisions about ORC itself recorded?
+
+`SCOPE.md` says facts about ORC belong in ORC's repository, yet ORC's architecture decision of 17 Sep is in this
+folder, ORC has no decision log, and the north star (25–26 Sep) is only in `STATE.md`.
+**Recommended:** here, in `decisions/`, as the 17 Sep decision already is; ORC's `AGENTS.md` keeps its standing rules
+and links here. Then the north star is copied here and `AGENTS.md`'s "Where a learning goes" table gains a row for
+decisions.
